<title>USA: Consolidated Natural files $950 mln shelf.</title>
<headline>Consolidated Natural files $950 mln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Natural Gas Co filed Thursday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf offering of up to $950 million in debt securities, preferred and common stock.</p>
<p>Together with a previous offering, the Pittsburgh based public utility holding company's shelf offering totals $1 billion.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale of the securities will be used to finance capital expenditures and other corporate needs.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the filing.</p>
</text>
